[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mRaise AWS PVM Production Documentation Fidelity\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Deliver epic `VFhICYohO` so Port's foundational and user-facing docs converge on one clear AWS production narrative with an explicit x86_64 hosted Firecracker/PVM lane. (\u001b[2mVFhICYohO\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Root contracts such as `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `CONFIGURATION.md` make it obvious which AWS deployment path is strongest today, which lane is still a repo-local proof, and which boundaries remain explicit. (\u001b[2mreview foundational docs for one coherent AWS/PVM production story\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - Focused guides and public docs explain AWS host-kit requirements, artifact-kit requirements, `prepare-pvm-node`, canonical machine launch/status/stop, and provider-aware failure surfaces without forcing operators to stitch together multiple contradictory pages. (\u001b[2mreview `docs/hosted.md`, `docs/cloud.md`, `docs/pvm.md`, and the public AWS docs path\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-04\u001b[0m - Scope stays documentation-only and truthful: no runtime claims beyond the current Port contract, no arm64 PVM promise, and no implied AWS infrastructure automation beyond Port's hosted lane. (\u001b[2mreview planning and docs artifacts for explicit scope boundaries\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFhICYohO\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - AWS PVM Production Documentation Contract (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-04-02T21:15:46\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFhICYWhN/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Raise AWS PVM Production Documentation Fidelity - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Deliver epic `VFhICYohO` so Port's foundational and user-facing docs converge on one clear AWS production narrative with an explicit x86_64 hosted Firecracker/PVM lane. | board: VFhICYohO |\r\n| MG-02 | Root contracts such as `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `CONFIGURATION.md` make it obvious which AWS deployment path is strongest today, which lane is still a repo-local proof, and which boundaries remain explicit. | manual: review foundational docs for one coherent AWS/PVM production story |\r\n| MG-03 | Focused guides and public docs explain AWS host-kit requirements, artifact-kit requirements, `prepare-pvm-node`, canonical machine launch/status/stop, and provider-aware failure surfaces without forcing operators to stitch together multiple contradictory pages. | manual: review `docs/hosted.md`, `docs/cloud.md`, `docs/pvm.md`, and the public AWS docs path |\r\n| MG-04 | Scope stays documentation-only and truthful: no runtime claims beyond the current Port contract, no arm64 PVM promise, and no implied AWS infrastructure automation beyond Port's hosted lane. | manual: review planning and docs artifacts for explicit scope boundaries |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Simplify the documentation map instead of adding another overlapping AWS narrative.\r\n- Keep AWS x86_64 hosted PVM as the strongest production-oriented cloud story without hiding that the standard hosted lane still exists.\r\n- Preserve current product truth: Port owns the runtime, host-kit, artifact-kit, and hosted control-plane contract, but not EC2 provisioning, IAM, VPC wiring, DNS, or downstream GitOps.\r\n- Keep GCP, Azure, and arm64 PVM boundaries explicit rather than inheriting the AWS contract by implication.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while operators still need to read several conflicting pages to understand the AWS PVM production path.\r\n- HALT when epic `VFhICYohO` is done and only manual mission verification remains.\r\n- YIELD if the remaining blocker is a product decision about whether AWS `standard` or AWS `pvm` should be the primary public production narrative.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFhICYohO\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mAWS PVM Production Documentation Contract\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 21:03:36\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 21:06:03\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 21:15:41\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-02 21:15:41\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m9m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFhICYohO/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFhICYohO/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port's documentation mentions hosted AWS and the PVM lane across README, foundational docs, focused guides, and the public docs site, but the production narrative is fragmented, duplicative, and still mixed with repo-proof language instead of one clear operator contract.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Converge Port's foundational documentation on one obvious AWS deployment narrative. (Root docs point readers to one canonical AWS/PVM path instead of repeating fragmented or conflicting guidance. -> One coherent root doc map)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Make AWS x86_64 hosted Firecracker/PVM the clearest production-oriented cloud narrative Port publishes today. (The docs distinguish the AWS PVM production lane from the standard hosted demo lane and from repo-local proof mechanics. -> One explicit AWS PVM operator contract)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Keep shipped boundaries honest while improving fidelity. (The docs remain explicit about missing provider automation, arm64 limits, and non-AWS boundaries. -> No accidental over-claims)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Root docs must direct readers to one canonical AWS production narrative instead of scattering the contract across multiple overlapping summaries.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFhIVMVEF\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - The docs must explain the AWS x86_64 hosted Firecracker/PVM lane as the strongest production-oriented Port narrative, including host kit, artifact kit, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mprepare-pvm-node\u001b[0m, and canonical machine lifecycle verbs.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFhIVMVEF\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - The docs must distinguish the AWS PVM lane from the hosted standard lane and from repo-local proof harnesses without hiding those surfaces.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFhIVMVEF\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Failure boundaries must stay explicit, including missing host kit, missing PVM artifacts, arm64 research-only status, and no silent inheritance to GCP or Azure.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFhIVMVEF\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The documentation set must become easier to navigate by reducing repeated AWS/PVM explanations and strengthening cross-links to a canonical path.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFhIVMVEF\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Public and root docs must stay aligned on the same AWS production posture.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFhIVMVEF\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Focused guides: Manual review of hosted, cloud, and PVM docs\r\n    - Public narrative alignment: Manual review of the Docusaurus AWS docs\r\n    - Root documentation: Manual review of the updated foundational docs\r\n\r\n\u001b[